dxmt: Complete an occlusion query that ends in a chunk without visibility results.

An occlusion query is completed by the visibility-result readback of the command chunk it ends
in, when that chunk finishes on the GPU. A chunk that recorded no visibility results made no
readback, so a query that began in one chunk and ended in another with no draws of its own after
a flush was never issued again, and GetData returned S_FALSE for it forever.

Such a chunk now makes a readback too, with no results and no buffer (Metal makes no buffer of
length 0, and no render pass of that chunk binds one), so the queries that end in it are issued
in order, after the chunks before it.

LOCAL TO THIS PORT, NOT FOR DXMT. Applied by macos/build-dxmt.sh to
github.com/athei/dxmt at 01e59e9bde030f105937f249afaac92ada01b4d7, after 0001 to 0006.
Written with an AI assistant (Claude). DXMT does not accept contributions made or
co-authored by AI (its CONTRIBUTING.md), so this patch must not be sent to it as a pull
request. What was found may be reported to its developers, for them to write their own fix;
this patch leaves here when the pinned commit has one.
---
diff --git a/src/dxmt/dxmt_context.cpp b/src/dxmt/dxmt_context.cpp
index 79d171e..6e546c2 100644
--- a/src/dxmt/dxmt_context.cpp
+++ b/src/dxmt/dxmt_context.cpp
@@ -1172,7 +1172,12 @@ ArgumentEncodingContext::flushCommands(WMT::CommandBuffer cmdbuf, uint64_t seqId
 
   QueryReadbacks readbacks{};
 
-  if (auto count = vro_state_.reset()) {
+  // A query that ends in this chunk is completed by this chunk's readback, also when the chunk
+  // recorded no visibility results: without one it was never issued again, and GetData never
+  // returned S_OK for it
+  auto count = vro_state_.reset();
+  if (count || std::any_of(pending_queries_.begin(), pending_queries_.end(),
+                           [=](auto &query) { return query->queryEndAt() == seqId; })) {
     readbacks.visibility = std::make_unique<VisibilityResultReadback>(
         device_, seqId, count, pending_queries_
     );
diff --git a/src/dxmt/dxmt_occlusion_query.hpp b/src/dxmt/dxmt_occlusion_query.hpp
index 839674b..c7f8233 100644
--- a/src/dxmt/dxmt_occlusion_query.hpp
+++ b/src/dxmt/dxmt_occlusion_query.hpp
@@ -171,10 +171,14 @@ public:
       queries(queries) {
         visibility_result_heap_info.options = WMTResourceHazardTrackingModeUntracked;
         visibility_result_heap_info.memory.set(nullptr);
+        visibility_result_heap_info.length = num_results * sizeof(uint64_t);
+        // a chunk with no results still issues the queries that end in it, with no buffer
+        // (Metal makes no buffer of length 0, and no render pass binds one)
+        if (!num_results)
+          return;
 #ifdef __i386__
         visibility_result_heap_info.memory.set(wsi::aligned_malloc(num_results * sizeof(uint64_t), DXMT_PAGE_SIZE));
 #endif
-        visibility_result_heap_info.length = num_results * sizeof(uint64_t);
         visibility_result_heap = device.newBuffer(visibility_result_heap_info);
       }
   ~VisibilityResultReadback() {
@@ -182,7 +186,8 @@ public:
       query->issue(seq_id, (uint64_t *)visibility_result_heap_info.memory.get(), num_results);
     }
 #ifdef __i386__
-    wsi::aligned_free(visibility_result_heap_info.memory.get());
+    if (num_results)
+      wsi::aligned_free(visibility_result_heap_info.memory.get());
 #endif
   }
 
